00:00:00,681 --> 00:00:14,691
1 / 7  •  FRAUD REVIEW WORKBENCH
Prioritize recorded transactions for human review. Synthetic PaySim v2; all services run locally.

2
00:00:14,691 --> 00:00:31,739
A REPRODUCIBLE MODEL AND REVIEW POLICY
Frozen features and model version. Top 100 reviews per simulation day; ranking scores are not probabilities.

3
00:00:31,739 --> 00:00:45,753
2 / 7  •  MEASURED OFFLINE RESULTS
Champion: 1,189 of 4,250 positives found at 100/day. The amount/type rule found 670.

4
00:00:45,753 --> 00:00:59,992
SIMULATOR LIMITATIONS STAY VISIBLE
Many hours contain only fraud-labelled rows. Mixed-hour hits: 505 of 2,000; no real-bank savings claim.

5
00:00:59,992 --> 00:01:20,214
3 / 7  •  A CAPACITY-LIMITED ANALYST QUEUE
Day 15: ranked alerts, simulation units and explicit missing-history indicators.

6
00:01:20,214 --> 00:01:39,242
4 / 7  •  EVIDENCE FOR THIS CASE
The case records its scoring step and review cutoff. Model associations are not proof of fraud.

7
00:01:39,242 --> 00:01:57,359
COMPUTED FACTS AND KNOWN GAPS
Source-linked facts are separated from missing device, identity and customer information.

8
00:01:57,359 --> 00:02:14,464
HISTORY AT SCORING VS. EVIDENCE AT REVIEW
A second case shows earlier recipient records and later review-time records in separate sections.

9
00:02:14,464 --> 00:03:15,681
5 / 7  •  LIVE LOCAL INVESTIGATION ASSISTANT
One case, read-only evidence tools and a fixed cutoff. This generation is shown in real time.

10
00:03:15,681 --> 00:03:39,716
CHECKED ANSWER, VISIBLE REFERENCES
The system-added scope line is distinct from model text. The assistant did not change the case.

11
00:03:39,716 --> 00:03:47,216
6 / 7  •  THE HUMAN MAKES THE DECISION
Start review, add an analyst note, and close with “needs more information.” No fraud label is asserted.

12
00:03:47,216 --> 00:03:56,468
A HUMAN DISPOSITION, RECORDED EXPLICITLY
Review is in progress. The analyst chooses “needs more information” without asserting a fraud outcome.

13
00:03:56,468 --> 00:04:08,863
AN APPEND-ONLY REVIEW TRAIL
The audit records the human actor, the previous state and the closed case disposition.

14
00:04:08,863 --> 00:04:25,863
7 / 7  •  REPRODUCIBLE, WITH HONEST LIMITS
101 tests pass. Fresh assistant holdout: 10/12; its two documented failures produced no unsafe delivered output.

15
00:04:25,863 --> 00:04:39,875
KNOWN ASSISTANT LIMITATIONS
Question-number filtering, refusal grading and short note paraphrases need further work. A small holdout is not a universal safety claim.

